<title>CHINA: China clears 4 more foreign banks for yuan trade.</title>
<headline>China clears 4 more foreign banks for yuan trade.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has approved four more foreign banks for dealing in local currency, the official China Daily said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the four are U.K.-based Standard Chartered Plc's Standard Chartered Bank unit, Japan's Sanwa Bank and Daiichi Kangyo Bank and the Shanghai-Paris International Bank, a joint venture between France's Banque National de Paris and the Industrial and Commerical Bank of China.</p>
</text>
